cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the U-STFT software, please cite the accompanying paper (preferred-citation below)."
title: "Universal Short-Time Fourier Transform (U-STFT)"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mananmittal/Universal-Short-Time-Fourier-Transform"
url: "https://mananmittal.github.io/Universal-Short-Time-Fourier-Transform/"
abstract: >-
  The U-STFT is a short-time Fourier transform whose window length adapts to
  the signal over time. At every frame it scores a dyadic bank of Gaussian
  windows by their normalized Rényi-3 time-frequency concentration, tracks a
  posterior over window lengths with a stay/grow/reset Markov prior, and
  outputs the posterior-weighted spectrum. A companion coefficient stream
  reconstructs the input exactly by overlap-add, so it can be filtered and
  resynthesized. Matching NumPy and PyTorch implementations are provided.
keywords:
  - short-time Fourier transform
  - STFT
  - spectrogram
  - time-frequency analysis
  - adaptive window length
  - Rényi entropy
  - signal processing
  - bioacoustics
  - PyTorch
